+# FAA OIG records schedule: signed approval face and later citation
+
+November 14, 2026 UTC · B129 / PD04–PD05. This is an additive visual review of the approval face of a previously acquired schedule. It supplements the [November 5 records-disposition crosswalk](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a00004833a29c648eb6d0cc7b3e2758b7eef2861/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-oig-records-disposition-crosswalk-2026-11-05/README.md); it does not change the earlier report or establish the disposition of the FAA case file.
+
+## Observations and provenance
+
+- The NARA-hosted [signed SF 115, physical page 2](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0398/n1-398-00-001_sf115.pdf#page=2), gives handwritten job number **N1-398-00-1**, receipt date **12-8-99**, agency certification date **12-2-99**, and an archivist approval date visually read as **10-4-00**. These dates were read from the page image; the PDF's extracted text does not reliably recover them. The attachment on [physical page 3](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0398/n1-398-00-001_sf115.pdf#page=3) is headed DOT Office of Inspector General, Investigative Case Files; item 1b gives an inactive-file cutoff and a ten-year period, with separately described significant cases excluded. The 2021 cover sheet calls the schedule **N1-398-00-001** and reports item 1b superseded; the sheet is distinct from the signed face.
+- The [July 20, 2012 Federal Register notice, physical page 4, printed page 42800](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2012-07-20/pdf/2012-17696.pdf#page=4), instead cites **N1–398–02–1, March 3, 2002**, for OIG investigative case files and describes a ten-year cutoff scheme and separately scheduled significant cases. The prior crosswalk reports that its captured NARA index did not contain that identifier under three tested spellings.
+
+## Interpretation and uncertainty
+
+The dates and job numbers are **separate observations attached to separately identified sources**. The 2012 notice does not establish that the pictured 2000 form is the authority it meant to cite. Overlapping subject matter and disposition wording alone cannot establish that the two identifiers refer to the same schedule. The 2012 citation could refer to an independently approved schedule or reflect a citation problem; neither explanation has been tested. No conclusion about deliberate alteration, retention, disposal, or concealment follows from this comparison.
+
+The handwritten date reading is a visual transcription, not independently authenticated metadata. The original signed 2002 authority, any amendments, authoritative crosswalk and case-specific schedule assignment remain unacquired. The 2006 case closure entry does not establish the case's disposition, an applicable cutoff, or whether a significant-case classification or hold applied. Preserve the earlier 2000 and 2012 system-notice retention descriptions and their differing triggers exactly as recorded in the predecessor review.
+
+## Open records and discriminating checks
+
+- [ ] Locate the complete signed **N1–398–02–1** authority and its approval face, amendments and any cross-reference to **N1-398-00-1 / N1-398-00-001**; compare original identifiers, approval dates, covered series and supersession history.
+- [ ] Obtain the OIG case-specific schedule designation, cutoff, significant-case decision, retention holds, transfer/receipt and any actual disposition records for **042R0122001 / CC-2006-085**. No disposal is inferred.
+- [ ] Obtain the corrected answer and receipt, signed action/no-action decision and recommendation-level history. This comparison supplies none of those records.
+
+## Reading and verification scope
+
+Two previously acquired public PDFs were rehashed; source URLs, acquisition and reexamination dates, SHA-256 values and byte counts are in [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json). The signature page was rendered with `pdftoppm -f 2 -l 2 -scale-to 2200 -png -singlefile` and visually inspected; the 2012 notice and source records were compared at the linked pages. A bounded web search for the 2012 identifier returned that notice and mirrors, but did not locate the signed authority; this is not an exhaustive search or proof it does not exist. The separate Treasury OIG report found during searching refers to the Department of the Treasury, so it supplies no demonstrated Transportation OIG system history.
